alwaysApply: true
---
This is an actively evolving computational neuroscience research codebase.

Priorities:
- clarity over cleverness
- minimal abstractions
- zero unnecessary redundancy
- code readable by neuroscientists

Assume the model will change.
Optimize for ease of modification, not architectural purity.

Prefer:
- small, composable functions
- explicit data flow
- simple control logic

Avoid:
- premature optimization
- heavy design patterns
- metaprogramming

Tests define the scientific contract of the model. They must never be modified implicitly or as a side effect of refactoring or cleanup commands